{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1otuYD8RVr36TguYRYP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I've signed off on the shop, gear and bestiary sweep, but with low confidence (0.4). I filed two reports and the developer replied \"could not reproduce\" to both, so neither is confirmed.\n\n**Reports filed, not confirmed:**\n- **Sell Old Gear total:** The preview showed a total of 5,416, but the visible rows add up to 5,198, a 218 gap. The sheet seems to hide its last row, probably Steel Full Helmet, and the list doesn't scroll. I saw it twice, including after closing and reopening the sheet.\n- **Bosses tab count:** The header read \"0 / 100 encountered\", the same as the Enemies tab, although only 7 bosses are listed.\n\n**Checked and consistent:**\n- Sell Junk preview, including with \"Keep one of each item\" on (I turned it off again afterwards).\n- The Iron Sword trade-in panel: 3 owned, 1 equipped, 2 sellable for 124 coins.\n- The gear slot chooser order for Body and Head: ranked by required level, then by title.\n- Attack, Strength and Defense totals before and after equipping and unequipping a helmet.\n- The Bestiary Missing, A–Z and By Location views and the item detail sheet.\n\n**Not tested:**\n- Buying anything in the shop.\n- Actually completing a bulk sale.\n- Rotating the screen.\n- The Bestiary after an enemy has been encountered.\n- The quest board beyond a quick look at the Gathering and Crafting lists, which looked consistent.\n\nTwo things looked odd but I didn't report them. The Bestiary A–Z list first showed only Vine Beast to Zombie, and on reopening it started at Abyssal Guardian as expected. In the Iron Sword trade-in the quantity chips read 1, 60, 180 and Max."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 380, "cache_read_input_tokens": 69318, "cache_creation":